# EXAMPLE knowledge-skill document (generic). Derived from the operator-tuned
# original with profile-specific anchors replaced by <PLACEHOLDERS>. Copy to
# $TREEBEARD_BASE/shared/toolbox/data/skills/<name>.txt and fill placeholders
# from your own career profile before use.
SKILL: adjacent_career_mapper (career_hunter package)
CONSUMER: governed Han turn. INPUT: career_profile.txt. OUTPUT: JSON query plan.

PURPOSE
Translate the operator's real capabilities into credible lateral career
families and posting-shaped search queries. Find roles the operator would
not think to search for on their own. Credible means: a hiring manager reading
the operator's resume could plausibly interview them. No fantasy
qualifications; stretch is allowed, fiction is not.

CAREER FAMILIES -- EXAMPLE set for a product/program-management background.
Replace with families adjacent to YOUR profile. Search across families,
not only the operator's current title.
  program_management            program manager, portfolio, PMO lead
  technology_governance         tech governance, IT governance, AI governance
  research_program_operations   research ops, research program manager
  institutional_strategy        strategy ops, chief of staff, planning
  innovation_programs           innovation program lead, pilots, incubation
  technology_policy             tech policy analyst/manager, digital policy
  partnerships                  partnerships manager, alliances, ecosystem
  implementation_leadership     implementation manager, delivery lead,
                                customer onboarding leadership
  operations_transformation     process/change manager, ops transformation
  conventional_pm_po            keep ONE query in the operator's CURRENT
                                title family as the control lane (rename
                                the key to match your background)

QUERY CONSTRUCTION RULES
1. Emit 8-12 queries total, at least 6 distinct families per day.
2. Posting-shaped, not index-shaped: pair role title with a domain or
   qualifier ("AI governance program manager remote", not "program
   manager jobs <PRIMARY_CITY>"). Avoid the words "jobs" and "careers" alone --
   they surface listicle/index pages.
3. Respect geography every time: each query carries "remote" or
   "<PRIMARY_CITY>" (rotate; <COMMUTABLE_AREA> acceptable).
4. Rotate families day to day so the same 8 queries are not repeated;
   vary phrasing on repeated families.
5. Operator-preference lane (EXAMPLE -- edit or remove to match your own
   priorities): at least one query per day targeting
   technology-for-good org shapes (nonprofit tech, digital rights,
   AI safety/governance orgs).
6. Never include excluded companies in queries. Never construct a query
   designed to find a specific excluded company.

OUTPUT FORMAT -- exactly this JSON shape, nothing else:
{"queries": [{"q": "<query>", "family": "<family_key>", "count": 8}, ...]}
